1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,540
Amen.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:52,760
Good morning.

3
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:55,440
How are y'all doing this morning?

4
00:00:55,440 --> 00:00:58,480
I love the energy.

5
00:00:58,480 --> 00:00:59,980
So grateful to be here.

6
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,200
I am committing what I call a preacher's cardinal sin this morning.

7
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:06,640
And it's not the denim jacket, I know.

8
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:09,340
I know some of you are thinking that it's the denim jacket.

9
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:09,780
It's not.

10
00:01:09,780 --> 00:01:17,820
I am preaching a sermon right as I get back from vacation, which means I am so rested and

11
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:20,480
rejuvenated that you guys should have packed a lunch.

12
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:21,400
I hope you did.

13
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:24,720
We're going to be here for a while.

14
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:26,560
No, I'm kidding.

15
00:01:26,980 --> 00:01:31,820
We are wrapping up our series on the summer in the Psalms.

16
00:01:31,940 --> 00:01:35,780
It's our last Sunday on the summer of Psalms.

17
00:01:35,780 --> 00:01:39,000
It's also our first Sunday back for many of our college students.

18
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,200
I saw some of you already.

19
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:41,860
I'm so glad that y'all are back.

20
00:01:41,860 --> 00:01:44,020
So excited to see you all over here.

21
00:01:44,020 --> 00:01:44,560
Yes.

22
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:48,400
Bring in the energy, the youth, the vitality.

23
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:52,120
And they will probably talk to me afterwards about the denim jacket.

24
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:53,240
We'll get it straightened out.

25
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:56,120
I'll figure out what's cool again, and it'll be great.

26
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:59,720
But like I said, we're wrapping up our series on the Psalms.

27
00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:05,520
We said that the Psalms is primarily a book that speaks for us rather than speaking to us.

28
00:02:05,520 --> 00:02:07,100
Most of the Scripture speaks to us.

29
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:13,740
The Psalms give us language that we can then take and reclaim and use back to God in our prayers.

30
00:02:14,380 --> 00:02:18,560
We've been doing kind of a mini-series on the Psalms of Ascent towards the end of this series.

31
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:31,920
The Psalms of Ascent are what most scholars agree on, are this group of psalms that they would sing as the nation of Israel made their three pilgrimages to Jerusalem for the three festivals that the Lord laid out for them to come.

32
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:39,980
This is a collective playlist that they would sing together as they made their journey to Jerusalem.

33
00:02:39,980 --> 00:02:49,700
And we intentionally put these at the end because we are getting ready to transition in this fall into a series on community and service.

34
00:02:49,700 --> 00:02:52,460
And we will be launching our small groups.

35
00:02:52,460 --> 00:02:57,580
And so I wanted to remind us at the end of this psalm series that the Scriptures really are a communal book.

36
00:02:57,760 --> 00:03:02,600
This is not just a book for you to read in your individual devotional life between you and God.

37
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:05,360
This is a book for us to read together in community.

38
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:14,060
And so if you don't have community, if you're not plugged into a smaller group of people, it doesn't have to be a canvas-sanctioned small group.

39
00:03:14,060 --> 00:03:22,700
But if you are not plugged into a group of believers that you can read the Scriptures with together in a circle and not just in a row, we want to encourage you to find that.

40
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:27,500
We have some new small groups launching here in just a few weeks, some small groups that have lots of openings.

41
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,700
That you can join in with a brand new crew of people.

42
00:03:30,700 --> 00:03:36,420
We also have a regular rhythm of small group that meets here on Sunday nights for new people.

43
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:37,140
It's every other week.

44
00:03:37,140 --> 00:03:37,840
It's not this Sunday.

45
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:38,640
It'll be next Sunday.

46
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:42,260
So we want you to find your people that you can read the Scriptures with together.

47
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:46,500
You can also sign up for passages classes where you can get together in smaller groups.

48
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:51,740
This is something that we believe wholeheartedly at our church, that we don't want people to just show up.

49
00:03:51,740 --> 00:03:53,100
It's great if that's your first step.

50
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:56,940
If you're testing this whole thing out, if you're dipping your toe in the water, that's great.

51
00:03:57,040 --> 00:03:57,540
Keep coming.

52
00:03:57,540 --> 00:03:59,640
Don't worry about getting in a circle yet.

53
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:01,760
But eventually, that is our goal for all of you.

54
00:04:01,760 --> 00:04:02,580
Sound good?

55
00:04:02,580 --> 00:04:04,340
All right.

56
00:04:04,340 --> 00:04:07,580
And I don't think it's a coincidence.

57
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:14,140
I think it's God's timing that I am scheduled to preach a psalm that is focused on Christian unity.

58
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:23,440
This morning, the same week that I need to address some concerns that I have received from some of you that others in our leadership have received from some of you.

59
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:29,160
So before we hop into the text, we have some housekeeping to do as a community.

60
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:30,220
Does that sound okay?

61
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:31,420
It'll be short, I promise.

62
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:41,080
But I don't think it's a coincidence that we are about to hop into a psalm focused on the unity of God's people when we need to address this issue.

63
00:04:41,080 --> 00:04:51,080
I have had several people who have come to me and others in our leadership who are concerned about the Blazing Hope fundraiser that we announced because it includes a alcohol.

64
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:51,820
Yes.

65
00:04:51,820 --> 00:04:52,780
And that's good.

66
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:56,720
It's important that we have these conversations as community.

67
00:04:56,720 --> 00:05:07,640
And so first and foremost, I want to thank all of you that came to me or another person on our leadership team directly with any concerns or questions or confusion that you might have.

68
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:17,860
Because as we get into unity, we're going to realize that true unity, real unity around the gospel of Jesus only happens when we're willing to have these conversations face-to-face, person-to-person.

69
00:05:17,860 --> 00:05:18,620
Right?

70
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:25,460
And so if you have come to us with your concerns, your questions, your confusion, I am so thankful for you.

71
00:05:25,460 --> 00:05:35,140
If you have come to other people behind the backs of leadership with confusion, questions, concerns, that's fine.

72
00:05:35,140 --> 00:05:37,600
But please come to us directly in the future.

73
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:38,960
We love to have these conversations.

74
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:41,720
We're not afraid to have conversations.

75
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:43,080
I'm not afraid to be wrong.

76
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:45,960
I am wrong multiple times a day.

77
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:46,320
Okay?

78
00:05:46,960 --> 00:05:50,140
So please, don't be afraid to come to me or our leadership.

79
00:05:50,140 --> 00:05:53,800
You all, our membership selects our board members.

80
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:59,680
So you have picked these people that help us make decisions and that you can come to with questions and concerns.

81
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:01,760
So thank you so much for doing that.

82
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:09,400
And secondly, I personally, as the leader of this group in some way, shape, or form, we are a collective leadership team.

83
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:11,720
But me, a lot of the brunt falls on me.

84
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:16,960
I want to apologize to you for the confusion that this fundraiser has caused for some of you.

85
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:23,480
And I want to give you some clarity on the why so that we understand, like, how we got to the decision that we made.

86
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:31,600
Because I think sometimes the why helps us have empathy and understanding, even if we don't fully agree with the decision, that we can have empathy with the people who made the decisions.

87
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:32,960
Does that sound fair?

88
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:42,340
So as Andy talked about this morning, Blazing Hope is a nonprofit Christian organization that we heavily support in their mission of restoring women survivors of sex trafficking.

89
00:06:42,340 --> 00:06:44,140
Can we all yes and amen that mission?

90
00:06:44,140 --> 00:06:45,360
Yes.

91
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:45,940
Thank you.

92
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:51,380
A large part of their funding for the entire year, they do this annual fundraiser.

93
00:06:51,380 --> 00:06:54,560
It's a banquet that they hold on a regular, an annual basis.

94
00:06:54,560 --> 00:07:02,480
And unfortunately, this year, the staff person who was in charge of planning that event left their organization abruptly and unexpectedly,

95
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:09,140
leaving them unable to hold this event that helps them raise the funds for their entire year's budget.

96
00:07:09,140 --> 00:07:10,100
And so they scrambled.

97
00:07:10,100 --> 00:07:13,000
They reached out to other organizations that support them.

98
00:07:13,300 --> 00:07:21,280
And they said, would you be willing to hold many banquets in your town, in your area, to help us recoup the funds that we're going to lose from this fundraiser?

99
00:07:21,280 --> 00:07:26,840
And a number of our church members stepped up in a pinch to help them plan this event.

100
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:30,900
They used a common playbook for nonprofit fundraisers that included a cash bar.

101
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:38,960
And I believe a lot of the confusion, frustration, questions came when we kind of advertised this as an event that our church was putting on.

102
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:40,480
That's my fault.

103
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:42,960
It's not our church putting on this event.

104
00:07:43,220 --> 00:07:45,340
It is blazing hope putting on this event.

105
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:51,420
And many of our members joined in to help them pull this off, which we are so thankful for each of you that did that.

106
00:07:51,420 --> 00:07:58,280
We, as an organization, believe that alcohol consumption is an issue of the conscious for the believer.

107
00:07:58,280 --> 00:07:59,900
It's addressed in Romans 14.

108
00:07:59,900 --> 00:08:02,120
I preached an entire sermon on it a while ago.

109
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:04,140
I'm going to share that in the newsletter this week.

110
00:08:04,140 --> 00:08:17,720
If you want more context on these issues of conscious and how we should treat one another in the midst of disagreements on disputable matters, please check that out and come to me with any questions or challenges that you have.

111
00:08:18,260 --> 00:08:20,880
I would highly encourage you to check that out.

112
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:31,440
It also, I was going to share it before I even decided to do this because it's a more practical application to my message on Psalm 133 that we're about to get into.

113
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:41,600
We decided to make this opportunity available to our people because it's an opportunity to help meet the needs of one of our ministry partners who is doing crucial gospel work.

114
00:08:42,100 --> 00:08:51,180
If an event with a cash bar is not something that you're able to attend because of your conscience or the price of the event is too much, we still want you to help support Blazing Hope.

115
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:53,080
There are volunteer options.

116
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:56,440
You can donate any dollar amount directly to them.

117
00:08:56,440 --> 00:08:57,900
We would love for you to support them.

118
00:08:57,900 --> 00:09:06,600
And finally, I want to remind us of Paul's words in 1 Corinthians where he states that I became all things to all people that I might win some.

119
00:09:07,260 --> 00:09:25,360
That the gospel motivates everything that we do in seeking to reach people and a huge majority of the events that our church people are involved in do not include alcohol intentionally because we want our church to be accessible and hospitable to those who struggle with alcoholism, those who avoid alcohol because of their conscience.

120
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:31,160
However, at times there are events our people are involved in that do include alcohol.

121
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:39,340
And I want to remind us that these events provide opportunities for us to bridge a cultural gap with people who would never come to our church on a Sunday morning.

122
00:09:39,340 --> 00:09:49,360
There are people who would never feel comfortable showing up to this space just yet, but there are environments that they will show up to with their questions about Jesus.

123
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:55,300
And I just want to remind us that the gospel that Paul says, I became all things to all people that I might win some.

124
00:09:55,380 --> 00:09:59,720
So we as an organization want to be hospitable and find ways to bridge cultural gaps.

125
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:12,860
And lastly, I want to remind us of a few of other Paul's words in Romans 15 where he says, accept one another then just as Christ has accepted you in order to bring praise to God.

126
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:22,260
So we are getting ready to hop into a sermon on unity and I realize that there's tension in this issue and that is okay, we're allowed to disagree about things like this.

127
00:10:22,260 --> 00:10:29,780
But in our disagreement, may we remember to accept one another as Christ has accepted you in order to bring praise to God.

128
00:10:29,780 --> 00:10:38,140
Because what we're going to find out in our text this morning is that unity, Christian unity is the primary motivation that's going to bring praise to God to the world around us.

129
00:10:38,140 --> 00:10:38,500
Sound good?

130
00:10:38,500 --> 00:10:43,340
All right, let's pray and we'll do the thing that I actually get paid to do, which is preach a sermon.

131
00:10:43,340 --> 00:11:02,100
All right, Father in heaven, we thank you that there is one body, one Lord, one Savior, one faith, one baptism, one God and Father over all who unites us in Christ Jesus.

132
00:11:03,300 --> 00:11:11,940
God, all of us have temptations and struggles and things that we deal with on a regular basis that seek to lead us away from obedience to you, God.

133
00:11:11,940 --> 00:11:14,240
And we want to have nothing to do with those temptations.

134
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:18,500
We want to run in obedience to you.

135
00:11:18,500 --> 00:11:23,820
And God, we want to be bridge builders to people who are outside of your church.

136
00:11:23,820 --> 00:11:28,520
We want to do that in a healthy way, in a way that models obedience to all of your creation.

137
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:35,160
We want to eat food and we want to do everything we do for the glory of God and the good of our neighbor.

138
00:11:35,160 --> 00:11:40,160
And God, when we seek to do that, we will make missteps.

139
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:42,100
We will screw up.

140
00:11:42,100 --> 00:11:44,220
May we have grace for one another.

141
00:11:44,220 --> 00:11:47,740
And may we find unity in the gospel of Jesus.

142
00:11:47,740 --> 00:11:50,740
That is the bridge that brings all sinners back to God.

143
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:53,360
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

144
00:11:53,360 --> 00:11:54,280
Amen.

145
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:57,280
Thank you all for letting me do that.

146
00:11:57,280 --> 00:11:58,860
And again, please talk to me.

147
00:11:58,860 --> 00:11:59,660
Talk to our leadership.

148
00:11:59,660 --> 00:12:01,820
We'd love to have conversations with you.

149
00:12:01,820 --> 00:12:06,440
If you have your Bible, Psalm 133 is going to be our psalm for the day.

150
00:12:06,440 --> 00:12:07,260
It is three verses.

151
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:07,940
It is short.

152
00:12:07,940 --> 00:12:12,880
It is easy to understand and, as you will see, hard to apply.

153
00:12:14,140 --> 00:12:28,500
As I was meditating on, studying this passage, I stumbled across an article in Time magazine that I think provides a helpful summary to some of the biggest issues that we are facing in our current cultural moment.

154
00:12:28,980 --> 00:12:34,860
To summarize, the author of this article argues that Americans are busy.

155
00:12:34,860 --> 00:12:38,400
Can anybody yes and amen that Americans are busy?

156
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:40,140
All right.

157
00:12:40,140 --> 00:12:42,240
Americans are busy.

158
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:43,440
We're working long hours.

159
00:12:43,440 --> 00:12:45,780
We're running from extracurricular to extracurricular.

160
00:12:45,780 --> 00:12:49,200
This business, this busyness creates loneliness.

161
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:54,200
Can anybody else yes and amen that many of us are lonely?

162
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:55,920
The statistics would back this up.

163
00:12:55,920 --> 00:12:56,520
We are busy.

164
00:12:56,520 --> 00:12:57,540
We are lonely.

165
00:12:57,540 --> 00:12:59,100
We don't have meaningful relationships.

166
00:12:59,100 --> 00:13:03,020
This loneliness causes us to look for microwave connections online.

167
00:13:03,020 --> 00:13:14,720
Algorithms create digital echo chambers, and we are never really exposed to people who disagree with us because our algorithms feed us what we want to hear.

168
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:18,040
And so we think that everyone agrees with every opinion that we have.

169
00:13:18,040 --> 00:13:23,540
Anybody yes and amen this as the current cultural temperature of our day?

170
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:28,780
The result is that we are an extremely divided culture of lonely and isolated people.

171
00:13:29,920 --> 00:13:35,520
I don't know about you, but I feel like the author is on to something in this article.

172
00:13:35,520 --> 00:13:44,940
And although I think we're facing loneliness and division in some unique ways in our current cultural moment, this is not a new problem.

173
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:57,240
From our fall in the garden, the beginning of the first book of the Bible, the people that God made to live in unity with himself and with one another have become divided.

174
00:13:57,240 --> 00:14:02,660
We've separated from God, and we've separated from one another, immediately blame-shifting, right?

175
00:14:02,660 --> 00:14:08,640
Adam and Eve are like, the woman you gave me, the snake that's here in this garden that you allowed to be here, right?

176
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:13,840
We blame-shift, we isolate, and it doesn't take very long for us to start killing each other.

177
00:14:13,840 --> 00:14:16,000
Genesis chapter 4, right?

178
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:25,480
Four chapters into God's good creation, his building us together in a garden, unifying us with one another and with him.

179
00:14:25,480 --> 00:14:30,200
And at the fall, we all started to move away from God and move away from one another.

180
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:34,480
And since the fall, the good news is that God has been moving back towards us.

181
00:14:34,480 --> 00:14:45,660
He invites individuals to form a new community, first the nation of Israel and then the church, centered around two primary commands, to love God and to love one another.

182
00:14:45,660 --> 00:14:58,980
This group of people was intended to be a counter-witness to the divided and isolated culture around us, a priesthood, inviting God's image-bearers back into relationship with him and fellowship with one another.

183
00:14:59,100 --> 00:15:04,600
That God has been moving towards us and our division of dividing against him and dividing against one another.

184
00:15:04,600 --> 00:15:13,860
He has been moving towards us and he has been inviting individuals back into relationship with himself and that we would cultivate a community where we're united with one another.

185
00:15:13,860 --> 00:15:19,180
And that would be a counter-witness to the divided world around us.

186
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:39,140
So with all of that as a backdrop, I don't think you would find it shocking to realize that one of the final songs on this playlist, the Psalms of Ascent playlist, as they're traveling together, this divided group of people that have been invited to be unified around the God of the Old Testament, Yahweh, that they are moving towards him.

187
00:15:39,140 --> 00:15:49,760
It's funny, it's funny, it's not funny, it's beautiful, that God forces them to come together three times a year to remind themselves of what they're really united about.

188
00:15:50,240 --> 00:16:09,340
And in this playlist of songs that they're moving towards Jerusalem, it's no shocker that David writes a specific song about unity, reminding them of what their primary directive is.

189
00:16:09,880 --> 00:16:20,620
That they are intended to remind themselves that they were created for fellowship with one another and with God.

190
00:16:20,620 --> 00:16:29,480
So, can we stand and read Psalm 133 together as an example of our unity?

191
00:16:29,480 --> 00:16:34,700
I'd love it if you all just read the whole thing with me.

192
00:16:34,700 --> 00:16:37,820
It's only three verses, so we should be able to knock it out.

193
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:41,520
This is a song of the ascents of David.

194
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:48,220
Verse one, how good and pleasant it is when God's people live together in unity.

195
00:16:48,220 --> 00:16:58,720
It is like a precious oil poured on the head, running down on the beard, running down on Aaron's beard, down on the collar of his robe.

196
00:16:58,720 --> 00:17:06,980
It is as if the dew of Hermon were falling on Mount Zion, for there the Lord bestows his blessings.

197
00:17:07,280 --> 00:17:09,440
Even life forever more.

198
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:10,860
Amen.

199
00:17:10,860 --> 00:17:11,640
You be seated.

200
00:17:16,020 --> 00:17:19,580
So, the thesis of David's song is pretty clear in verse one.

201
00:17:19,580 --> 00:17:26,400
David is saying, it is good and pleasant when God's people dwell in unity.

202
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:31,900
I actually, because I was on vacation, I finished my sermon on Monday, so there are notes in the bulletin this week.

203
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:35,420
If you like that kind of thing, you can follow along with the notes on the back.

204
00:17:35,420 --> 00:17:37,640
But David's thesis is pretty clear.

205
00:17:38,400 --> 00:17:41,320
It is good and pleasant when God's people dwell in unity.

206
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:45,760
It is rare and difficult, but it is worth the effort that is required.

207
00:17:45,760 --> 00:17:52,200
And David goes on to use two poetic images that work both on a practical and a spiritual level.

208
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:52,960
Don't you love Scripture?

209
00:17:53,760 --> 00:18:01,220
It's obvious on the surface, but if you keep digging deeper, there's even more truth to be mined out from these two images.

210
00:18:01,380 --> 00:18:07,300
The first image is this, that unity is pleasant like a sweet-smelling perfume.

211
00:18:07,300 --> 00:18:12,440
On a practical level, precious oil was a luxury in this world.

212
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:19,660
It was moisturizing and sweet-smelling in a world where baths were hard to come by, right?

213
00:18:19,660 --> 00:18:28,400
We got dirty, sun-dried, leathery human beings, and oil is hard to come by.

214
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:31,500
Only wealthy people would have access to this.

215
00:18:31,500 --> 00:18:34,020
This oil would refresh their skin.

216
00:18:34,020 --> 00:18:38,760
It would moisturize them, and it would bring pleasant-smelling aromas all around them.

217
00:18:38,760 --> 00:18:43,720
The oil would be noticeable to everyone around them for days.

218
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:52,480
At the practical surface level application here, David is saying that when God's people dwell in unity,

219
00:18:52,480 --> 00:18:54,920
it becomes pleasant and enticing.

220
00:18:54,920 --> 00:18:59,960
It is an aroma, a sweet-smelling aroma to everyone around us.

221
00:18:59,960 --> 00:19:04,920
It is refreshing and encouraging, and it noticeably changes the environment around us.

222
00:19:08,120 --> 00:19:12,840
Anointed people have something rare that others around them do not.

223
00:19:12,840 --> 00:19:17,800
And the question at this point in the message that we should be pondering is,

224
00:19:17,800 --> 00:19:22,540
are we cultivating a type of unity that is noticeable to those around us?

225
00:19:22,540 --> 00:19:27,620
Is our unity rare to the world that is isolated and divided?

226
00:19:27,620 --> 00:19:29,260
And if not, why?

227
00:19:29,260 --> 00:19:31,080
It's what David is saying.

228
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:37,040
Christian community is intended to be something that you can't get anywhere else.

229
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:42,380
It's something that you need, that you long for, that even if you don't know you need it,

230
00:19:42,380 --> 00:19:44,240
when it walks in the room, you realize it.

231
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:51,920
And as a called-out priesthood of believers that find themselves in Christ's church,

232
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:58,560
are we cultivating a unity, a relationship, a depth of unity that people around us,

233
00:19:58,560 --> 00:20:01,360
people outside these walls, people who aren't plugged into churches,

234
00:20:01,360 --> 00:20:03,980
are they looking at our relationship with one another?

235
00:20:03,980 --> 00:20:07,680
The way that we handle difficult conversations about disagreements?

236
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:10,260
The way that we handle disunity?

237
00:20:10,260 --> 00:20:15,680
Are we creating the type of unity that is pleasant and sweet-smelling to those around us?

238
00:20:15,680 --> 00:20:17,540
Is it rare?

239
00:20:19,160 --> 00:20:22,000
And if not, why?

240
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:28,300
Are we missing out on one of the primary directives that we have been invited to participate in

241
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:33,460
by not cultivating this unity that is pleasant and rare and sweet-smelling to the world around us?

242
00:20:33,460 --> 00:20:35,740
Very practical application.

243
00:20:35,740 --> 00:20:38,780
But David takes it a step deeper.

244
00:20:39,620 --> 00:20:43,160
And this image becomes not just practical, but spiritual.

245
00:20:43,160 --> 00:20:45,840
He's not just talking about any oil.

246
00:20:45,840 --> 00:20:51,060
He's talking about a very specific oil on a very specific person.

247
00:20:51,060 --> 00:20:56,640
He's talking about the anointing oil that would anoint Aaron as the high priest.

248
00:20:56,640 --> 00:21:03,400
This is an oil that was, there was a special recipe for this oil given directly from God to Israel

249
00:21:03,400 --> 00:21:07,260
for the purpose of anointing the tabernacle and the priests.

250
00:21:07,980 --> 00:21:09,720
And I love how Tim Mackey puts it.

251
00:21:09,720 --> 00:21:15,680
He argues that part of the significance of this oil is that it is the life of Eden compressed.

252
00:21:15,680 --> 00:21:20,380
It is all of God's good creation compressed into liquid form,

253
00:21:20,380 --> 00:21:28,380
and it is used by God to set people apart and set places apart to be a holy,

254
00:21:28,380 --> 00:21:32,460
a distinct bridge between heaven and earth.

255
00:21:32,460 --> 00:21:36,660
So the tabernacle became a bridge between heaven and earth.

256
00:21:36,800 --> 00:21:39,400
We've been divided from God, divided from one another.

257
00:21:39,400 --> 00:21:44,900
And the tabernacle and the priest were these intentional symbols set up to bridge the gap

258
00:21:44,900 --> 00:21:49,280
between heaven and earth, to unify heaven and earth.

259
00:21:49,280 --> 00:21:58,980
David isn't just arguing that God's people living in unity is like a pleasant aroma,

260
00:21:59,140 --> 00:22:09,740
but that when we dwell in unity, we are set apart, holy, functioning as representatives who are becoming a bridge that connects heaven to earth.

261
00:22:09,740 --> 00:22:14,740
Our unity is intended to be a bridge to connect heaven to earth,

262
00:22:14,740 --> 00:22:19,280
to show all of the people, all of the image bearers of God,

263
00:22:19,360 --> 00:22:25,560
what God intended in his creation, that we would be connected to him and connected to one another in unity.

264
00:22:25,560 --> 00:22:31,980
But this is where the reality of life comes face to face with the beautiful imagery of this song.

265
00:22:32,040 --> 00:22:37,820
I think all of us would agree with and pursue this reality as a general hypothetical pursuit, right?

266
00:22:37,820 --> 00:22:40,440
All of us would say, yeah, unity is pleasant.

267
00:22:40,440 --> 00:22:41,520
It is nice.

268
00:22:42,520 --> 00:22:43,560
It's wonderful.

269
00:22:43,560 --> 00:22:46,700
Everyone around us, we just know about it when we walk in.

270
00:22:46,700 --> 00:22:48,140
We should pursue this.

271
00:22:48,140 --> 00:22:53,140
But what about when I start naming the specific types of people

272
00:22:53,140 --> 00:23:01,260
with the specific opinions on meaningful things like theology, politics,

273
00:23:01,260 --> 00:23:07,760
and name your pet peeve subject or topic, right?

274
00:23:07,760 --> 00:23:10,640
We all agree unity is pleasant, like sweet-smelling perfume,

275
00:23:10,640 --> 00:23:15,120
but what if I started listing the names of people, the types of people with the types of opinions?

276
00:23:15,120 --> 00:23:19,000
Would it be as exciting to pursue?

277
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:21,860
It gets hard real quick, right?

278
00:23:21,860 --> 00:23:26,920
And I think this is baked into David's imagery.

279
00:23:26,920 --> 00:23:32,380
He says it's like a precious oil poured on the head, running down onto the beard,

280
00:23:32,380 --> 00:23:34,420
Aaron's beard, right?

281
00:23:34,420 --> 00:23:35,220
Very specific.

282
00:23:35,220 --> 00:23:38,620
The high priest is running down on the high priest's beard,

283
00:23:38,620 --> 00:23:40,320
down on the collar of his robe.

284
00:23:40,320 --> 00:23:42,280
You can almost see the imagery, right?

285
00:23:42,280 --> 00:23:44,800
Starts on the head, it's moving down to the beard,

286
00:23:44,800 --> 00:23:46,560
it's moving down from the beard to the collar.

287
00:23:46,560 --> 00:23:49,900
Where would it move next after it rolled down the collar?

288
00:23:49,900 --> 00:23:52,240
Just imagine this with me.

289
00:23:52,240 --> 00:23:54,980
As I was meditating on this imagery,

290
00:23:54,980 --> 00:23:59,200
I just saw the oil dripping from the collar to the chest of the robe.

291
00:23:59,200 --> 00:24:01,380
And those of you that know your Old Testament,

292
00:24:01,380 --> 00:24:02,920
you know what's on Aaron's chest.

293
00:24:02,920 --> 00:24:04,860
Does anybody remember what's on Aaron's chest?

294
00:24:06,340 --> 00:24:09,220
12 stones for the 12 tribes of Israel.

295
00:24:09,220 --> 00:24:13,980
And I can just hear the people of Israel bemoaning this imagery.

296
00:24:13,980 --> 00:24:18,660
Like, yes, unity, sweet smelling, perfume, it's dripping down.

297
00:24:18,660 --> 00:24:23,960
And then immediately they're confronted with the fact that David is talking about unity

298
00:24:23,960 --> 00:24:26,400
between all the 12 tribes of Israel.

299
00:24:29,200 --> 00:24:33,640
Very diverse group of people with very diverse opinions and culture

300
00:24:33,640 --> 00:24:35,360
about all kinds of different things.

301
00:24:35,360 --> 00:24:37,540
I think we're so removed from the culture.

302
00:24:37,540 --> 00:24:38,040
We're like, what?

303
00:24:38,040 --> 00:24:39,760
They're one nation?

304
00:24:39,760 --> 00:24:42,200
They all stem from one family?

305
00:24:42,200 --> 00:24:44,480
It should be easy for them to be unified, right?

306
00:24:48,220 --> 00:24:52,120
We're talking about 12 sons from four different mothers.

307
00:24:52,120 --> 00:24:54,820
Any blended families in here?

308
00:24:54,820 --> 00:24:56,900
Yeah?

309
00:24:56,900 --> 00:24:57,560
Unity?

310
00:24:57,560 --> 00:24:58,260
Easy?

311
00:24:58,260 --> 00:25:02,460
We all think alike, we all act alike, we all talk alike, right?

312
00:25:02,460 --> 00:25:08,120
No, this is not a group of people that would find it easy to be unified with one another.

313
00:25:08,120 --> 00:25:10,060
They're spread out geographically.

314
00:25:11,460 --> 00:25:21,560
I use ChatGPT to tell me what state in America would be like the closest to the size of biblical Israel, New Jersey.

315
00:25:21,560 --> 00:25:24,180
My wife's from New Jersey.

316
00:25:24,180 --> 00:25:26,860
She's from South Jersey.

317
00:25:26,860 --> 00:25:34,060
South Jersey and North Jersey are very different places with very different types of people.

318
00:25:34,060 --> 00:25:35,680
Just ask them.

319
00:25:35,680 --> 00:25:39,060
Just ask them, right?

320
00:25:39,800 --> 00:25:53,080
So what we're talking about here is we're not talking about some beautiful poetic imagery about a group of people who God just created in this special, unique place where he isolated them only with people who think exactly like them, where unity is easy and perfect to come by.

321
00:25:53,080 --> 00:26:01,240
We're talking about 12 sons from four different mothers displaced across the geography of the state of New Jersey.

322
00:26:01,240 --> 00:26:06,560
This is not easy to create unity with this group of people.

323
00:26:06,920 --> 00:26:09,780
We can take it out of the Old Testament into the New Testament.

324
00:26:09,780 --> 00:26:11,460
We can look at the disciples of Jesus.

325
00:26:11,460 --> 00:26:15,060
We've got fishermen, we've got tax collectors, and we've got zealots.

326
00:26:15,060 --> 00:26:23,380
These are not the type of people that would hang out at a pub together after a long day's work, right?

327
00:26:23,380 --> 00:26:27,860
These are people that if they had to choose, they would not go near each other.

328
00:26:27,860 --> 00:26:38,360
And yet the gospel of Jesus is calling them together around one unified table to create a unity that is pleasant and sweet-smelling like perfume to the world around us.

329
00:26:38,360 --> 00:26:39,360
This is not easy.

330
00:26:39,360 --> 00:26:46,520
This is not an echo chamber of people that have all of the same theology as you do and all of the same politics as you do.

331
00:26:46,600 --> 00:26:56,020
This is a diverse group of people that all find their unity around Jesus Christ, crucified, risen, ascended into heaven, and coming again.

332
00:26:56,020 --> 00:26:57,780
That is where our unity is found.

333
00:26:57,780 --> 00:27:00,240
And for many of us, that's all we have in common.

334
00:27:02,240 --> 00:27:10,700
And yet the directive is that we would be unified for the sake of the world around us.

335
00:27:10,700 --> 00:27:23,140
We move from the Old Testament to the disciples to the church, where in Galatians we find that Paul says the church is male, female, slave, free, Jew, Gentile.

336
00:27:23,140 --> 00:27:32,000
These categories of people could not have different mindsets or opinions about things, and yet Paul is saying your unity should be found in Jesus.

337
00:27:32,240 --> 00:27:38,120
I draw all of this out to say, I think most of us read things like Psalm 133.

338
00:27:38,120 --> 00:27:41,280
We find it beautiful and compelling, and we likely agree with the premise.

339
00:27:41,280 --> 00:27:46,160
But most of us settle for a much more watered-down application.

340
00:27:46,160 --> 00:27:59,160
We might be able to find somewhat meaningful unity with our tribe, but all the tribes, it's like, ah, these non-denominational people, they're pretty cool.

341
00:27:59,160 --> 00:27:59,800
They're chilling.

342
00:28:00,720 --> 00:28:02,620
They do fundraisers with cash bars.

343
00:28:02,620 --> 00:28:04,040
I can get down with them.

344
00:28:04,040 --> 00:28:05,760
Right?

345
00:28:05,760 --> 00:28:13,900
The Methodists, the Baptists, the Catholics who professed Christ, crucified, risen, and coming again.

346
00:28:13,900 --> 00:28:19,660
The Greek Orthodox who professed Christ, faith in Jesus.

347
00:28:19,660 --> 00:28:20,340
Right?

348
00:28:20,340 --> 00:28:22,660
Like, this is a big family.

349
00:28:22,660 --> 00:28:27,360
And oftentimes we settle for a watered-down version of unity.

350
00:28:27,700 --> 00:28:33,280
But David's prophetic charge to us this morning is that watered-down unity isn't a sweet-smelling aroma of Christ.

351
00:28:33,280 --> 00:28:40,020
Watered-down unity does not do the thing that the unity that God called us to do does.

352
00:28:41,220 --> 00:28:51,460
It is not a witness to the world around us if we just gather together with people who have the same exact theology as us and the same exact politics as us and come from the same exact demographic as us.

353
00:28:52,800 --> 00:28:54,880
This does nothing for the world around us.

354
00:28:54,880 --> 00:28:55,780
So, like, good for you.

355
00:28:55,780 --> 00:28:59,540
We have social clubs, too, where we all get together with people who agree with us.

356
00:29:05,440 --> 00:29:10,320
This type of unity does not set us apart to be a bridge between heaven and earth.

357
00:29:10,320 --> 00:29:14,900
So, what does watered-down unity look like?

358
00:29:14,900 --> 00:29:17,020
Just to get really practical, really quick.

359
00:29:17,020 --> 00:29:19,900
I told you I shouldn't preach after I get home from vacation.

360
00:29:19,900 --> 00:29:23,720
First, uniformity.

361
00:29:23,720 --> 00:29:24,800
Right?

362
00:29:24,880 --> 00:29:27,420
We create a unity where everyone just looks like us.

363
00:29:27,420 --> 00:29:31,860
Everyone votes like us, believes like us, talks like us, acts like us.

364
00:29:31,860 --> 00:29:36,460
This is not the type of unity that David is calling God's people to.

365
00:29:36,460 --> 00:29:43,660
The second type of watered-down unity that I think oftentimes we, I, struggle with more than that is avoidance.

366
00:29:44,500 --> 00:29:48,520
We're like, I have unity with people, but only because we never talk about the hard things.

367
00:29:48,520 --> 00:29:55,920
That's not the type of unity that David is prophetically inviting God's people to.

368
00:29:55,920 --> 00:29:58,640
It's not the type of unity that Christ has invited us to.

369
00:29:58,640 --> 00:30:08,100
We have to be willing to have the difficult conversations and find unity around Christ in the midst of our disagreements on things that are less important than Christ.

370
00:30:08,100 --> 00:30:09,160
Amen.

371
00:30:11,100 --> 00:30:17,260
The type of unity we are being invited into is centered on the life, death, resurrection, ascension, and coming again of Jesus.

372
00:30:17,260 --> 00:30:24,260
It invites us to become family with Christians living in both Israel and Palestine, Russia, and Ukraine.

373
00:30:24,260 --> 00:30:30,620
It invites both the wealthy business owner and the struggling mother to the single mother to the same communion table,

374
00:30:30,620 --> 00:30:36,340
the Democrat and the Republican, the Pentecostal, the Baptist, the Methodist, and the Mennonite,

375
00:30:36,340 --> 00:30:44,860
all finding common ground on Calvary's Hill for the sake of inviting the isolated and divided world around us to find salvation in Christ.

376
00:30:44,860 --> 00:30:52,880
For those of you that aren't super tapped into theological discussions,

377
00:30:52,880 --> 00:31:01,720
Pentecostal, Baptist, Methodist, and Mennonites have some pretty significant disagreements on some pretty meaningful things.

378
00:31:01,720 --> 00:31:05,380
Did that on purpose for those of you that are tapped in to be like, wait, what?

379
00:31:06,340 --> 00:31:08,780
Yes, that, unity in that.

380
00:31:08,780 --> 00:31:11,880
I'm reminded of the famous quote that says,

381
00:31:11,880 --> 00:31:16,980
in essentials, unity, in non-essentials, liberty, and in all things, charity.

382
00:31:16,980 --> 00:31:20,840
I am not saying that our differences of opinion, culture, and theology don't matter.

383
00:31:20,840 --> 00:31:22,780
I'm saying they don't matter as much as unity.

384
00:31:24,460 --> 00:31:31,100
David's prophetic song is an invitation for all God's people to do the hard work to cultivate unity amidst diversity

385
00:31:31,100 --> 00:31:38,960
so that we might be a sweet-smelling aroma to the world around us, set apart as a bridge between heaven and earth.

386
00:31:40,100 --> 00:31:45,540
He moves on from this imagery of anointing oil to this imagery of water.

387
00:31:45,540 --> 00:31:50,760
Second point I have here is unity is refreshing like water in a dry land.

388
00:31:50,760 --> 00:31:56,720
This image, just like the oil, works on a practical and a spiritual level, which we'll get into.

389
00:31:56,720 --> 00:32:01,280
First, on a practical level, I don't have to spend a lot of time explaining this.

390
00:32:01,360 --> 00:32:06,040
All of you have had a drink of ice-cold water after a long, hot day in the sun.

391
00:32:06,040 --> 00:32:07,780
We know how this works, right?

392
00:32:07,780 --> 00:32:15,880
Water brings life and vitality and rejuvenation to a dry and barren land.

393
00:32:15,880 --> 00:32:20,340
And David here says that unity is like the dew of Hermon.

394
00:32:20,340 --> 00:32:27,820
It's like as if the dew of Hermon were falling on Mount Zion, where the Lord bestows his blessing.

395
00:32:28,020 --> 00:32:31,440
Mount Hermon is in the northern boundary of biblical Israel.

396
00:32:31,440 --> 00:32:37,200
It's close to 7,000 feet higher in elevation than Mount Zion in Jerusalem, where the temple is.

397
00:32:37,200 --> 00:32:41,300
Because of its geography, it would have snow caps much of the year.

398
00:32:41,300 --> 00:32:46,480
Even as things got drier down below, the people of Israel would be able to look up and see the moisture,

399
00:32:46,480 --> 00:32:48,380
see the refreshing water.

400
00:32:48,380 --> 00:32:51,700
As the snow melted, it fed the springs that flowed into the Jordan River

401
00:32:51,700 --> 00:32:56,340
and provided much of the needed water for the dry and weary land.

402
00:32:57,520 --> 00:33:01,440
And the question that we should be asking ourselves at this point in the psalm is,

403
00:33:01,440 --> 00:33:06,360
are we cultivating a type of unity that is refreshing to those around us?

404
00:33:06,360 --> 00:33:11,460
That is like ice-cold water to a dry and weary land.

405
00:33:11,460 --> 00:33:16,200
If we agree with the premise that we are a busy, lonely, isolated people,

406
00:33:16,200 --> 00:33:21,560
are we as followers of Jesus doing the hard work to cultivate united relationships,

407
00:33:21,560 --> 00:33:26,840
deep, meaningful relationships that are like a fresh drink of water to the world around us?

408
00:33:27,020 --> 00:33:28,740
And if not, why?

409
00:33:28,740 --> 00:33:35,860
This image also goes beyond just the practical level.

410
00:33:35,860 --> 00:33:42,820
Notice he mentions, it's as if the dew of Mount Hermon were falling on Mount Zion.

411
00:33:42,820 --> 00:33:50,380
He says that God's people living in unity is if the dew from Mount Hermon would fall on Mount Zion.

412
00:33:50,500 --> 00:33:53,140
I'm not a scientist, so I had to do some research here.

413
00:33:53,140 --> 00:33:55,560
That's not possible.

414
00:33:55,560 --> 00:34:01,160
With how far away these two mountains were because of the geographical distance,

415
00:34:01,160 --> 00:34:06,420
this would be impossible for the water from Hermon to become dew on Mount Zion,

416
00:34:06,420 --> 00:34:08,660
apart from a miracle,

417
00:34:09,280 --> 00:34:12,200
which is what I want us to wrestle with this morning.

418
00:34:12,200 --> 00:34:19,160
Because I think God's people dwelling in unity is impossible apart from the miraculous work of the Holy Spirit.

419
00:34:19,160 --> 00:34:25,000
This is not something we can just bear down, grit our teeth, and do on our own.

420
00:34:25,000 --> 00:34:33,400
And we need the Holy Spirit to unify us together in the midst of our very tense and very meaningful disagreements.

421
00:34:38,000 --> 00:34:41,860
It would take a miracle for God's people to dwell in unity.

422
00:34:41,860 --> 00:34:46,560
But thanks be to God, we worship a God who does miracles.

423
00:34:46,560 --> 00:34:48,100
Right?

424
00:34:48,100 --> 00:34:53,640
Thanks be to God that we worship a God who raised Jesus from the dead,

425
00:34:53,640 --> 00:34:58,300
so I think he can take a couple of Democrats and a couple of Republicans and put them in the same small group.

426
00:34:58,300 --> 00:35:04,480
And maybe we would learn to love each other in the midst of our disagreements,

427
00:35:04,840 --> 00:35:08,860
because the thing that unites us is far more important than the thing that we disagree on.

428
00:35:08,860 --> 00:35:17,560
And let's not forget that some of the last words that we have recorded from Jesus before he goes to the cross

429
00:35:17,560 --> 00:35:20,140
is a prayer for his people to live in unity.

430
00:35:20,140 --> 00:35:25,020
Jesus prays for us to be miraculously united by the power of the Spirit.

431
00:35:25,020 --> 00:35:28,960
He says, so that the world around us will know that he is God.

432
00:35:28,960 --> 00:35:33,780
And I don't know what things you pray for,

433
00:35:34,780 --> 00:35:38,620
I typically don't pray for things that are probably going to happen even if I don't pray.

434
00:35:38,620 --> 00:35:40,300
Right?

435
00:35:40,300 --> 00:35:44,320
Like Jesus isn't praying for something that he thinks is just going to naturally happen.

436
00:35:44,320 --> 00:35:48,000
All of these united, male, female, slave free, Jew, Gentile,

437
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:50,640
they're just going to naturally fall into a united relationship.

438
00:35:50,640 --> 00:35:55,540
Jesus is praying for this because he knows it is going to take a miraculous work of the Spirit.

439
00:35:56,040 --> 00:36:07,620
He's inviting God the Father to send the Spirit to do a miraculous work amongst us so that we might be united so that the world around us will know that he is who he says he is.

440
00:36:08,880 --> 00:36:16,840
My main point for this morning in your notes is this, that God's people living in unity is a foretaste of the kingdom to come.

441
00:36:19,040 --> 00:36:20,780
This is what he says in verse 3.

442
00:36:20,780 --> 00:36:24,380
It's like dew of Hermon falling on Mount Zion.

443
00:36:24,380 --> 00:36:31,780
For this is where the Lord bestows his blessing, even eternal life, life forever more.

444
00:36:31,780 --> 00:36:36,620
Unity becomes a picture of what heaven will look like.

445
00:36:37,380 --> 00:36:48,480
We see this in Revelation 7, where people from every tribe, language, nation, and tongue are all unified before the throne of Jesus,

446
00:36:48,480 --> 00:36:54,480
crying out, salvation belongs to our God who sits on the throne and to the Lamb.

447
00:36:54,480 --> 00:37:02,800
Unity is a foretaste of the kingdom to come.

448
00:37:04,120 --> 00:37:12,080
Every tribe, every nation, every language, every tongue, all who have confessed faith and trust in Christ alone for salvation.

449
00:37:12,080 --> 00:37:15,440
I don't care what denomination they're a part of.

450
00:37:15,440 --> 00:37:18,040
I don't care what their political affiliations are.

451
00:37:18,040 --> 00:37:18,860
I mean, I care.

452
00:37:18,860 --> 00:37:28,000
We can have those conversations, but unity requires that we unite on the sake of the gospel.

453
00:37:29,160 --> 00:37:36,100
And all these other conversations we can and we should have, but we should have them reminding ourselves daily that unity is more important.

454
00:37:36,100 --> 00:37:45,900
That agreeing on being united around the shed blood of Jesus is more important than all of the other conversations that are important to have.

455
00:37:53,500 --> 00:38:00,440
So if you agree with the premise that unity in the midst of diversity is a foretaste of the kingdom to come,

456
00:38:00,440 --> 00:38:03,480
like a sweet-smelling aroma, like a refreshing drink of water,

457
00:38:03,480 --> 00:38:07,140
to this isolated, lonely, and divided world around us,

458
00:38:07,140 --> 00:38:12,120
then what can we do practically to cultivate this type of unity,

459
00:38:12,120 --> 00:38:18,520
this type of miraculous unity that only happens by the power of the Spirit working in each one of us?

460
00:38:22,160 --> 00:38:23,420
I created a list.

461
00:38:23,420 --> 00:38:24,940
That's what pastors do.

462
00:38:24,940 --> 00:38:27,880
It's not an exhaustive list.

463
00:38:27,880 --> 00:38:30,880
There's plenty more things that the Spirit might be telling you to do right now.

464
00:38:30,880 --> 00:38:32,580
Listen to the Spirit over my list.

465
00:38:32,580 --> 00:38:34,100
But if the list helps you,

466
00:38:34,100 --> 00:38:41,860
first, intentionally seek out relationships and conversations with brothers and sisters in Christ

467
00:38:41,860 --> 00:38:43,480
who have different perspectives than you.

468
00:38:43,480 --> 00:38:48,600
Look for these conversations.

469
00:38:48,600 --> 00:38:50,080
Seek them out.

470
00:38:52,020 --> 00:38:56,880
Many of you did that over the last few weeks with some of us about this issue of alcohol.

471
00:38:56,880 --> 00:38:58,380
And I'm so grateful you did.

472
00:38:58,380 --> 00:39:01,920
I think I'm a, I think iron sharpened iron in those conversations.

473
00:39:01,920 --> 00:39:06,620
And I still might be wronger than you want me to be, but I'm a work in progress.

474
00:39:06,620 --> 00:39:11,980
Intentionally seek out relationships and conversations with brothers and sisters in Christ

475
00:39:11,980 --> 00:39:13,520
who have different perspectives than you.

476
00:39:14,940 --> 00:39:15,440
I've got time.

477
00:39:15,440 --> 00:39:15,740
I've got time.

478
00:39:15,740 --> 00:39:17,100
So I'm going to give examples.

479
00:39:17,100 --> 00:39:21,700
Sometimes I put things in parentheses and I think there's no way I'm going to have time

480
00:39:21,700 --> 00:39:22,020
for this.

481
00:39:22,020 --> 00:39:24,060
So who cares how bold and audacious it is?

482
00:39:24,060 --> 00:39:25,860
And now I have time.

483
00:39:25,860 --> 00:39:26,740
So I have to do it.

484
00:39:26,740 --> 00:39:37,540
I grew up in a church, in a tribe of churches where women were not permitted to preach.

485
00:39:39,060 --> 00:39:42,040
And I grew up thinking that that was right because the Bible says so.

486
00:39:42,040 --> 00:39:48,120
And I grew up thinking that anybody who disagreed with that reality didn't care about the Bible

487
00:39:48,120 --> 00:39:49,240
because the Bible said so.

488
00:39:51,420 --> 00:39:56,880
And so I didn't have any desire to have any conversation with any brother or sister in Christ

489
00:39:56,880 --> 00:40:01,700
who had a woman preach at their church because I thought the Bible says so.

490
00:40:01,700 --> 00:40:05,300
So you must not care about the Bible.

491
00:40:05,300 --> 00:40:08,440
So we must not be able to be unified.

492
00:40:08,440 --> 00:40:11,760
Then I grew up a little bit.

493
00:40:11,760 --> 00:40:14,980
Just a little, just a little bit.

494
00:40:17,540 --> 00:40:22,960
And I looked for, I sought out conversations with people who disagreed with me because I

495
00:40:22,960 --> 00:40:27,300
saw that they were godly, that they loved the Lord, they loved the Scriptures.

496
00:40:27,300 --> 00:40:29,780
And I thought, maybe I'm missing something.

497
00:40:29,780 --> 00:40:35,640
And I had years and years of conversation with these people.

498
00:40:35,640 --> 00:40:42,040
And I think I might have changed their opinion about people who believed like me.

499
00:40:42,040 --> 00:40:46,220
And I know for a fact they changed my opinion about people who believed like them.

500
00:40:46,860 --> 00:40:52,040
And I know for a fact that I'd rather be united with them here and now as we wait for Jesus

501
00:40:52,040 --> 00:40:54,100
to come back and tell us which one of us is right.

502
00:40:54,100 --> 00:41:02,840
We need to get better at changing our mind about stuff.

503
00:41:02,840 --> 00:41:11,400
Second, acknowledge your own bias and lack of knowledge on the subject.

504
00:41:16,180 --> 00:41:18,700
Just realize that you come to the table.

505
00:41:18,700 --> 00:41:20,800
We all come to the table with a bias.

506
00:41:20,800 --> 00:41:24,860
I now believe that women can preach.

507
00:41:24,860 --> 00:41:29,180
And when I have that conversation with people who disagree with me, I have to acknowledge that

508
00:41:29,180 --> 00:41:29,980
I have a bias.

509
00:41:29,980 --> 00:41:35,020
That there are passages of Scripture that make it seem like that should not happen.

510
00:41:35,020 --> 00:41:38,340
And when I look at those passages, I look at them with a bias.

511
00:41:38,340 --> 00:41:42,280
And there are other passages that make it pretty clear that they should.

512
00:41:42,440 --> 00:41:47,460
And when my friends who disagree with me look at those passages, they look at it with a bias.

513
00:41:48,460 --> 00:41:54,600
And if we both pretend like we don't have biases and we are the only ones who have a monopoly

514
00:41:54,600 --> 00:42:00,080
on the truth of Jesus Christ, no progress towards unity will ever be found.

515
00:42:01,080 --> 00:42:10,840
And there are too many leaders of theological camps on both sides of that argument who lead their people to be arrogant and unaware of their biases.

516
00:42:14,600 --> 00:42:20,940
And we just need to be reminded that the Savior that we worship is the same Savior who stooped down.

517
00:42:20,940 --> 00:42:29,080
Before he was about to be raised from the dead, demonstrating that he is God in the flesh, he stooped down and washed his disciples' dirty feet.

518
00:42:33,280 --> 00:42:36,700
Let's acknowledge our biases and our lack of knowledge on the subject.

519
00:42:36,700 --> 00:42:40,900
Let's believe the best about the person you disagree with.

520
00:42:40,900 --> 00:42:42,440
To quote Ted Lasso.

521
00:42:42,440 --> 00:42:46,300
Be curious.

522
00:42:46,300 --> 00:42:48,500
Not judgmental.

523
00:42:48,500 --> 00:42:49,940
Right?

524
00:42:49,940 --> 00:42:52,160
Let's believe the best.

525
00:42:52,160 --> 00:42:56,260
Let's go into the conversation thinking maybe this person actually does love the Scripture.

526
00:42:56,640 --> 00:42:59,340
And maybe I have a biased opinion about them.

527
00:42:59,340 --> 00:42:59,920
Be curious.

528
00:42:59,920 --> 00:43:00,780
Not judgmental.

529
00:43:00,780 --> 00:43:05,120
And lastly, know the difference between an open-handed issue and a closed-handed issue.

530
00:43:05,120 --> 00:43:09,580
And be willing to be charitable and disagree about open-handed issues.

531
00:43:09,580 --> 00:43:15,180
We are united around closed-handed issues.

532
00:43:15,180 --> 00:43:16,920
We don't budge on those things.

533
00:43:16,920 --> 00:43:19,440
Christ Jesus, the Son of God.

534
00:43:19,440 --> 00:43:20,840
Sinless.

535
00:43:20,840 --> 00:43:22,580
Crucified.

536
00:43:22,580 --> 00:43:23,940
Risen and coming again.

537
00:43:23,940 --> 00:43:25,440
We do not budge on those things.

538
00:43:26,180 --> 00:43:29,240
If someone disagrees with that and they claim to be a follower of Jesus.

539
00:43:29,240 --> 00:43:32,800
We just treat them like they need to be introduced to Jesus.

540
00:43:32,800 --> 00:43:40,100
But if they agree with that and then disagree with us about every other meaningful topic in the world,

541
00:43:40,100 --> 00:43:41,420
they are our brother and sister.

542
00:43:41,420 --> 00:43:44,100
And that means we're forced to sit around the table with them.

543
00:43:44,100 --> 00:43:47,880
So we need to learn how to do it in unity for the sake of the world around us.

544
00:43:47,880 --> 00:43:54,220
We're going to conclude our service today by taking communion,

545
00:43:54,220 --> 00:43:58,440
which I think is the perfect reminder of what is open-handed and what is closed-handed.

546
00:43:58,440 --> 00:44:03,700
Closed-handed issues are the ones that give us access to the communion table.

547
00:44:05,060 --> 00:44:16,660
This regular practice that Jesus gave all of his followers, male, female, slave, free, Jew, Gentile, Democrat, Republican, Israeli, Palestinian, Ukrainian, Russian,

548
00:44:16,800 --> 00:44:28,500
and all who claim the name of Jesus are invited to the communion table if they profess faith and trust in Jesus crucified, risen, and coming again.

549
00:44:29,780 --> 00:44:38,080
This regular practice that Jesus gave us becomes like the three pilgrimages for the nation of Israel.

550
00:44:38,600 --> 00:44:54,540
As 12 tribes all gathered together at this one central location, as they had to look each other in the eye and realize that you're from Benjamin, I'm from Judah, right?

551
00:44:54,540 --> 00:45:04,700
Diverse groups of people with different opinions, and they all were forced to come together to remind themselves that what unites them is far more important than what divides them.

552
00:45:05,460 --> 00:45:08,520
And the communion table becomes that for us, brothers and sisters.

553
00:45:08,520 --> 00:45:18,180
Becomes this place where we meet together with people of diverse backgrounds, diverse opinions, diverse theological perspectives,

554
00:45:18,180 --> 00:45:34,840
and we take the body of Christ, and we partake in it, because that is the thing that unifies us, and that is the thing that is going to save the lonely, isolated world around us.

555
00:45:34,840 --> 00:45:43,040
Not our politics, not our economics, not our whatever your thing might be.

556
00:45:43,040 --> 00:45:50,380
The thing that will save us is Christ Jesus crucified, buried, risen, ascended to the throne, and coming again.

557
00:45:50,380 --> 00:45:57,480
So I'm going to pray, and I'm going to dismiss you for communion.

558
00:45:57,480 --> 00:46:03,660
If you haven't been here when we do this table communion, it's chaos, organized chaos.

559
00:46:03,660 --> 00:46:06,420
It's part of the thing that unites us.

560
00:46:06,420 --> 00:46:07,740
So we'll put a map up on the screen.

561
00:46:07,900 --> 00:46:12,580
If you're new here, just follow the person in front of you and pretend like you know what you're doing, and you'll probably get communion.

562
00:46:12,580 --> 00:46:22,620
Communion at Canvas is that we participate in open communion, which means we don't stand at the table and tell you if you can or can't take it.

563
00:46:23,120 --> 00:46:32,320
But I do want to tell you up front right now that this is a thing that is only for people who have placed their faith and trust in Jesus alone for salvation.

564
00:46:32,320 --> 00:46:36,180
And if you're here and you're just questioning, you're wrestling, you've got your doubts, that's okay.

565
00:46:36,180 --> 00:46:37,060
Please keep coming.

566
00:46:37,060 --> 00:46:46,240
But the Scriptures are clear that you're about to do a thing that acknowledges that a man lived on earth, and that man was God.

567
00:46:47,300 --> 00:46:51,900
And he died, and he rose again, and he's coming again.

568
00:46:51,900 --> 00:46:55,540
And so if you can't claim that, don't take this yet.

569
00:46:55,540 --> 00:46:57,320
Just keep wrestling, keep asking.

570
00:46:57,320 --> 00:47:01,200
And nobody's going to judge you for not coming down, okay?

571
00:47:01,200 --> 00:47:05,320
And if they do, tell me, and I'll have one of those hard conversations that I don't like to have.

572
00:47:05,320 --> 00:47:07,780
All right.

573
00:47:07,780 --> 00:47:08,880
Let's pray.

574
00:47:09,020 --> 00:47:32,700
Father in heaven, thank you for this psalm that reminds us where our unity is found, that reminds us of the beauty, the hope, and the chaos that is unifying with a diverse group of people around the central truth of all creation,

575
00:47:32,700 --> 00:47:36,520
that we have been separated from you, but that you are coming for us.

576
00:47:38,520 --> 00:47:45,380
God, I pray this morning that your Holy Spirit did exceedingly abundantly more than I could ask, think, or imagine, that you are restoring relationships,

577
00:47:45,380 --> 00:47:53,140
that you are prompting people to go and have conversations with one another over things that they've been stewing over for months or even years.

578
00:47:53,140 --> 00:47:55,760
God, may forgiveness happen.

579
00:47:55,760 --> 00:47:57,420
May restoration happen.

580
00:47:57,420 --> 00:47:58,400
May healing happen.

581
00:47:58,400 --> 00:48:08,140
And may this group of people under this roof be unified in such a way that is like a sweet-smelling aroma, like a fresh drink of water to the world around us.

582
00:48:09,340 --> 00:48:11,560
In Jesus' name I pray, amen.
